{% set local_problems %}
<p>Scottsboro presents two distinct gutter challenges: the humid lakeside environment and the aging housing stock in town.</p>

<p>Properties near Lake Guntersville experience elevated humidity levels that standard aluminum gutters handle well — but the fascia boards and wood trim around them don't fare as well. We see more rot and water damage per capita in lake-area homes than almost anywhere else in our service area. Homes that sit vacant during off-seasons are especially vulnerable, since small problems go unnoticed until they become expensive repairs.</p>

<p>Meanwhile, many homes in downtown Scottsboro and the surrounding neighborhoods were built in the 1950s-70s. These older homes often have original gutters that have long outlived their useful life — rusted, sagging, or held together with increasingly desperate patches. Replacing these aging systems with modern seamless gutters protects the homes and preserves their character.</p>

<p>Whether you're maintaining a lakeside retreat or preserving a piece of Scottsboro history, Blue River Gutters has the experience to help. We understand the unique challenges here and provide solutions built to last.</p>
{% endset %}

